{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 3010,
    "dDurationMs": 3990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thanks to Brilliant.org for supporting PBS Digital Studios."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7500,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To repeat the Space Time maxim: It's never aliens..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11500,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "... until it is!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13000,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, let's talk about 'Oumuamua."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20500,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Last year, a visitor came to our inner Solar System."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24000,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To us, it looked like a faint spot of light, moving quickly relative to the fixed stars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29050,
    "dDurationMs": 2450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We'd seen similar things countless times before:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31500,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lonely rocks, remnants of the formation of our Solar System,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35500,
    "dDurationMs": 5550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "drifting on their endless orbits around the Sun, and faintly glimmering with its reflected light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41050,
    "dDurationMs": 2950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Nothing unusual about such asteroids and comets,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44000,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but what made this object special was its trajectory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48000,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was not in orbit around the Sun at all."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50500,
    "dDurationMs": 5500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Rather, it appeared to have fallen in from interstellar space, and was on its way back out again."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56000,
    "dDurationMs": 7500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The object is 1I/2017 U1 -- better known as 'Oumuamua."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63500,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's the first chunk of interstellar space debris we've ever spotted passing through our Solar System."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70500,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It caused a justifiable stir at the time -- hell, even we did an episode on it!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75500,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But 'Oumuamua has been making the news again."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79000,
    "dDurationMs": 9000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This time, it's for a new paper by Schmuel Bialy and Avi Loeb that investigates the possibility that 'Oumuamua is..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88000,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "... aliens!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 89500,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or, more accurately, an artificial light sail, presumably attached to an alien probe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94570,
    "dDurationMs": 3430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Today on Space Time Journal Club, I want to do two things."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98000,
    "dDurationMs": 6500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, assess the plausibility of this proposal, and second, talk about the media hype around it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104500,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First up, here's what we know about 'Oumuamua:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108000,
    "dDurationMs": 5500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Its changing brightness suggests it's a highly elongated object, tumbling through space."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 113500,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It appears to be a few hundred meters long, but only a few tens of meters across."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118000,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It may or may not also be flat."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120500,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's a space baguette, perhaps after going through a space sandwich press."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125000,
    "dDurationMs": 5349,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Initially, its reddish color looked comet-like, but then it didn't produce a cometary tail,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130420,
    "dDurationMs": 5580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so it was assumed it must be more rocky or asteroid-like, at least on the surface."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 136000,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A couple of strange things right there!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138000,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The geometry is very unusual for an asteroid or comet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 141500,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's also a little surprising that we should have seen an interstellar object at all."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 146000,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We certainly expect there to be a bunch of space junk floating between the stars,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 150000,
    "dDurationMs": 5500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "probably ejected in the violent early stages of formation of planetary systems."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 155500,
    "dDurationMs": 7500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in order for our encounter with 'Oumuamua to have been likely, that population needs to be huge --"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 163000,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "much more interstellar debris than our theoretical models predict."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 166500,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Those things are odd, but not odd enough to start assuming aliens."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171000,
    "dDurationMs": 5500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But now that 'Oumuamua is on its way out of the solar system, it's doing something even weirder:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 176500,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It appears to be accelerating."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179000,
    "dDurationMs": 5500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or, at least it's not slowing down as much as you'd expect due to the Sun's gravitational pull."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 184500,
    "dDurationMs": 5500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This non-gravitational acceleration was reported in a nature paper in June."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 190000,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The extra acceleration is tiny, but it's clear."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 194060,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Something is pushing the body outwards."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 197000,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By itself, this wouldn't be anything especially weird."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 200000,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Comets show the same sort of acceleration on their way out from the Sun."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 204000,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In their case, it's a result of outgassing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 207000,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As the Sun heats the rear surface of the comet, water ice and frozen gases -- so-called volatiles -- evaporate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 214000,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The ejected gases act like jets to propel the comet forward."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 218000,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In regular comets, the outgassing is typically visible as sunlight reflects off dust carried along with the jets,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 225050,
    "dDurationMs": 3950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and we see it as the comet's coma and tail."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 229000,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But no coma or tail was observed in 'Oumuamua."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 233000,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Also, outgassing should probably change the way the object is tumbling, but 'Oumuamua's tumbling appears consistent."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 240000,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So... duh... aliens, right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 242000,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So proposed Bialy and Loeb of Harvard University."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 246500,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To be fair, in the paper itself, these authors don't say it's aliens, or even that it's probably aliens."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 252560,
    "dDurationMs": 6440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They just do a few calculations to show the plausibility of one particular explanation:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 259000,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that 'Oumuamua is a light sail."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 262500,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the argument:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264000,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Something is accelerating this object with no visible coma or tail."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268000,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It doesn't look like outgassing, so maybe it's radiation pressure."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 273000,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Sun's own light could be pushing on the object, speeding it up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 276000,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, the observed acceleration seems to be following an inverse square law."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 281000,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The acceleration is decreasing with the square of the distance from the Sun."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 285000,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, that's exactly what you'd expect for solar radiation pressure."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 289000,
    "dDurationMs": 5500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Incidentally, this inverse square acceleration is also what you'd expect from outgassing,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 294500,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because outgassing also depends on the strength of the Sun's radiation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 298000,
    "dDurationMs": 5500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the radiation pressure thing would only work if 'Oumuamua is incredibly thin and light --"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 303500,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thinner and lighter than any conceivable natural space object."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 307000,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ergo... aliens!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 309000,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bialy and Loeb calculate that a 50 meter wide sheet less than a millimeter thick"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 313000,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and made of a highly reflective material would produce the observed brightness and acceleration."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 318000,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That sounds like a light sail."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 320500,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is technology that we are playing with already."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 323500,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Japanese IKAROS light sail flew to Venus in 2010"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 327000,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the Breakthrough Starshot program is planning to use a light sail as our first interstellar probe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 332000,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The light sail hypothesis potentially explains the acceleration and the weird shape."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 337000,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It may also explain why we saw something at all."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 340500,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Given that natural space debris the size of 'Oumuamua should be much rarer between the stars,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 346500,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what if this wasn't a chance encounter?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 349500,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What if aliens sent this probe to us intentionally?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 353000,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's review the evidence."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 355000,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "'Oumuamua appears to be accelerating out of the solar system in a way completely consistent with outgassing,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 361000,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "except there's no visible outgassing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 363000,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "'Oumuamua is weirdly shaped for a natural body,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 366500,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and there shouldn't be enough interstellar space junk for something like 'Oumuamua to have been spotted by chance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 372530,
    "dDurationMs": 6970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Regarding these unusual qualities, co-author Avi Loeb is fond of quoting Sherlock Holmes:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 379500,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"When you have excluded the impossible, whatever remains, however improbable, must be the truth.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 385500,
    "dDurationMs": 7500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The implication of that statement is that all other possible explanations for 'Oumuamua's weirdness have been ruled out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 393099,
    "dDurationMs": 1401,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, have they?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 394500,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's look at the non-alien explanations of 'Oumuamua's behavior."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 399500,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The acceleration is the weirdest thing, so we'll start there."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 403599,
    "dDurationMs": 4901,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Outgassing is the obvious alternative, but then, why don't we see it?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 408500,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, I mentioned that in regular comets the coma and tail are seen through sunlight reflected off dust --"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 415500,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tiny mineral grains that are carried out with the vaporizing ice."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 419500,
    "dDurationMs": 8000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Without reflective dust, outgassing would be invisible to our telescopes, but could still cause the observed acceleration."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 427500,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The paper that first reported the unusual acceleration proposes some plausible scenarios."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 433500,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Perhaps the object has a low abundance of dust."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 437000,
    "dDurationMs": 7500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or, perhaps it has unusually large dust grains that'd reflect less light than lots of smaller grains."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 444500,
    "dDurationMs": 7500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or, perhaps the surface material has been fused into a crust by millennia of exposure to interstellar cosmic rays."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 452000,
    "dDurationMs": 5500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The lack of visible outgassing is weird, but frankly, it's not that weird."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 457500,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Slightly weirder is that the tumbling motion doesn't seem affected by outgassing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 462580,
    "dDurationMs": 6420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But until someone does a proper calculation to show that tumbling must change in an observable way,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 469000,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this is not a serious argument."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 471000,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then there's 'Oumuamua's shape. How do you get such a weird shaped rock?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 476000,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, different authors have suggested different scenarios."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 479500,
    "dDurationMs": 6500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Perhaps it was tidally disrupted -- pulled apart by the star or a gas giant from its home system,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 486000,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "much like the comet Shoemaker-Levy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 489000,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then, it may have gravitationally reassembled itself into an odd shape on that very long interstellar journey."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 496000,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Loeb himself proposes a similar explanation in an earlier paper,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 500589,
    "dDurationMs": 5411,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "adding that perhaps it broke itself apart due to its rapid rotation before reassembling."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 506000,
    "dDurationMs": 5500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And finally, what about the sheer unlikelihood of a random encounter with an interstellar space rock?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 511500,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, in order for our spotting of 'Oumuamua to have been likely,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 516000,
    "dDurationMs": 8000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "interstellar space needs to contain something like 10 to 100 times the number of 'Oumuamua-like space rocks than we expect."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 524000,
    "dDurationMs": 6500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And by that, I mean the expected density of space rocks that are ejected during the planetary formation process."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 530500,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are three counter-arguments:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 533000,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, there could be more space debris than we expected."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 536500,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, it may be that stars release their Oort clouds when they die."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 541500,
    "dDurationMs": 5500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If every star that passed before us shed its vast cloud of comets into the galaxy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 547000,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that would make plenty enough interstellar trash to explain 'Oumuamua."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 552009,
    "dDurationMs": 1491,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Second explanation:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 553500,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Maybe we just got lucky with 'Oumuamua."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 556000,
    "dDurationMs": 6500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Maybe interstellar space junk is rare, but we caught a 0.1 or 1 or 10 percent chance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 562500,
    "dDurationMs": 8000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And finally, perhaps 'Oumuamua isn't from outside our solar system at all, but rather comes from our own Oort cloud,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 570500,
    "dDurationMs": 8000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and was socked from its orbit by impact and/or gravitational interaction into a trajectory that will send it to the stars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 578500,
    "dDurationMs": 6500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We can comfortably say that natural explanations for 'Oumuamua are still plausible."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 585000,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Can we really say the same about the unnatural explanation of an alien light sail?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 591000,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One thing the light sail doesn't explain is the tumbling motion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 595000,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Certainly, a working probe shouldn't be spinning end over end, so perhaps it's a broken probe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 601000,
    "dDurationMs": 5500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if so, then we have the same abundance problem as with natural interstellar debris."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 606500,
    "dDurationMs": 8000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Interstellar space would need to be filled with broken light sails -- something like 10^15 probes per star in the Milky Way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 614500,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The other issue with the light sail hypothesis is the speed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 619000,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "'Oumuamua was traveling at 26 kilometers per second before it entered our Solar System,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 624000,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that's a pretty typical speed for a random object orbiting in the Milky Way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 629000,
    "dDurationMs": 6500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On the other hand, the Breakthrough Starshot light sails are aiming at 20% light speed,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 635500,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for a 20 year journey to the Alpha Cent. system."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 638000,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's been a million years since 'Oumuamua's last stellar encounter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 643000,
    "dDurationMs": 8000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So why build a probe that travels at such a snail's pace, surely beyond the lifespan of any aliens who sent it?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 651000,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Especially when the technology to accelerate a light sail to a good fraction of the speed of light"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 655500,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is within the grasp of even us primitive humans."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 659010,
    "dDurationMs": 7990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's pretty safe to say that any unnatural explanation for 'Oumuamua is still less likely than a natural explanation,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 667000,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and honestly, I suspect that Bialy and Loeb know that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 670500,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In their paper, they don't claim that an alien light sail is the most likely explanation -- just that it's a plausible one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 677500,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The issue isn't that they did the analysis."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 680000,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Scientists should be free to pursue fringe ideas, as long as they do it scientifically."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 685000,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The issue is how this idea ended up being communicated to the public."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 690000,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So let's talk about that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 691500,
    "dDurationMs": 8500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The light sail hypothesis for 'Oumuamua was first presented by Avi Loeb in late September, in a Scientific American article."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 700000,
    "dDurationMs": 4580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A month later, the Bialy and Loeb paper appeared on the preprint arXiv,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 704580,
    "dDurationMs": 4420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and a few days after that, Centauri Dreams and Universe Today wrote about it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 709000,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Over the next couple of weeks, many media outlets picked up the story."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 713500,
    "dDurationMs": 3020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Some of those articles were measured, and some were even critical,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 716520,
    "dDurationMs": 4980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but most were giddy at the possibility that we'd discovered an alien craft."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 721500,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The credentials of the authors were blared in the headlines:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 724500,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"Harvard astrophysicists... blah blah blah... alien probe.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 728500,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While nothing in these articles was untrue, it's arguable that there's some dishonesty here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 733500,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The appeal to the authority of the authors seems designed to provoke the reaction,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 738500,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"Well, if Harvard scientists say so, then it must be true.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 742500,
    "dDurationMs": 6500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The author responses in media interviews do not downplay the likelihood of aliens."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 749000,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, that Sherlock Holmes quote."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 751060,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, my question to you:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 754000,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Is it harmful to emphasize an unlikely scientific interpretation beyond its probable veracity,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 760000,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just for the sake of clicks and attention,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 763000,
    "dDurationMs": 7500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or is any engagement of the public with science ultimately a good thing, as long as there's no clear harm?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 770500,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Honestly, I don't know the answer,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 773000,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but I do know that 'Oumuamua is one of the most fascinating discoveries in astronomy in recent times."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 780000,
    "dDurationMs": 8500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Whether or not it's aliens, it's likely our first encounter with the natural or unnatural denizens from interstellar space time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 789000,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Are you interested in learning more about astronomy?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 792000,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Brilliant is a problem-solving website that teaches you to think like a scientist."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 796500,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead of passively listening to lectures, you get to master concepts by solving fun and challenging problems."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 803500,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Brilliant provides the tools and framework you need to tackle these problems."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 808000,
    "dDurationMs": 6500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Brilliant's thought-provoking content, based around breaking up complexities into bite-sized understandable chunks"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 814500,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will lead you from curiosity to mastery."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 817500,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Whether you want to learn about astronomy, quantum physics, or even artificial neural networks,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 822000,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can learn more at brilliant.org/spacetime."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 826500,
    "dDurationMs": 6500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Last week, we talked about the possible detection of what may be the first supersymmetric particle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 833000,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, before I get to comments, I need to make one big correction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 837000,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thanks to Gustavo Valdiviesso for pointing this out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 840000,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I said that extremely high energy neutrinos aren't expected to make it all the way through the planet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 846000,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hence the surprise at seeing the decay products of a high-energy tau neutrino"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 851000,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that had appeared to pass right through the center of the Earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 854000,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This ain't right!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 855810,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Neutrinos have no trouble passing through the planet, whatever their energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 859500,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What changes is neutrino oscillations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 863500,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As a neutrino travels through empty space, they [sic] oscillate between the three types:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 868000,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "electron neutrino, muon neutrino, and tau neutrino."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 871000,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The rate of oscillation depends on the tiny mass of the neutrino."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 875500,
    "dDurationMs": 6060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When passing through matter, interactions with the electromagnetic field change the effective mass of the neutrino"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 881560,
    "dDurationMs": 5940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by a process analogous to the refractive index, which changes the speed of light in matter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 887500,
    "dDurationMs": 6500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This, in turn, changes the probabilities of oscillation, and suppresses oscillations to tau neutrinos."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 894000,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the Mikheyev-Smirnov-Wolfenstein (or MSW) effect."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 900000,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, it's not that neutrinos don't make it through the planet,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 903000,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's just that they don't oscillate into tau neutrinos or stay as tau neutrinos."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 907500,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So seeing a tau neutrino coming from directly below is incredibly unlikely."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 912000,
    "dDurationMs": 7500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hence, the hypothesis that it was an electron or muon neutrino that interacted to produce a supersymmetric stau particle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 920000,
    "dDurationMs": 8000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tu-nonna-emiliana asks: if SUSY is easy (just add an S to the start), then how about Sstring?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 928000,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, actually modern string theory relies on supersymmetry, so it's already included."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 934000,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Was it called \"ting theory\" before that?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 937500,
    "dDurationMs": 5500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Actually, the name string theory originally applied to what we call bosonic string theory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 943000,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It just explained the force carrying bosons like the graviton and the photon."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 947600,
    "dDurationMs": 5900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To encompass fermions, supersymmetry is needed. The result is superstring theory,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 953500,
    "dDurationMs": 5048,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and these days some form of superstring theory is implied when people talk about string theory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 959000,
    "dDurationMs": 5500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Many of you noticed a typo in the segment of the Wikipedia text that we put on screen for the hierarchy problem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 964500,
    "dDurationMs": 5500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It appeared to say that the weak force is 1,024 times stronger than gravity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 970000,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Some of you took that to be evidence for the simulation hypothesis."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 973529,
    "dDurationMs": 3971,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But actually, it's just that the exponent got lost in the cut and paste."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 977500,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It should have been 10 to the power of 24 times stronger."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 981000,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hiccup Haddock asks:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 982500,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Why ice?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 984120,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As in: Why does IceCube use photon detectors in ice instead of any other material?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 990000,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, the answer's simple enough: Ice is transparent(ish)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 994000,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Neutrinos are detected by the Cherenkov radiation produced by particles produced in neutrino collisions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1001000,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That radiation travels a short distance through ice to the nearest photon detector."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1005500,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The same interactions happen in rock, but the Cherenkov radiation doesn't get very far."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1010500,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You could use transparent materials other than ice."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1013000,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Liquid water is common, for example, in the Super-Kamiokande neutrino detector in Japan."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1018000,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I guess you could use a giant cube of glass or similar, but that sounds expensive."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1023000,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Many of you are impressed by Ice Cube's incredible contributions to particle physics,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1027500,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and how the guy has had such a diverse career."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1030500,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thanks to infectedstyles and David M for reminding me of Ice Cube's classic,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1035000,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"Straight Outta Lepton\", during his \"Neutrinos With Attitude\" years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1039079,
    "dDurationMs": 5921,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And some of you thought my \"or is it\" was very Vsauce."
    } ]
  } ]
}
